EN10338 

Small businesses are increasingly forced to build card processing fees into the price of every product because surcharging rules and consumer expectations make separate surcharges impractical. This means all Australians—including cash-paying customers—are paying higher prices while banks and payment providers continue to profit from payment processing. This petition calls on Parliament to introduce reforms that shift these costs away from businesses and consumers and onto the financial institutions that already profit from electronic transactions. 

We therefore ask the House to amend Australia's payment system and consumer protection laws to reduce or eliminate merchant payment processing fees on everyday debit and credit card transactions; 

require payment providers and financial institutions to offer low-cost electronic payment services that do not impose unnecessary costs on Australian businesses and consumers; 

direct the relevant regulators to review the impact of card payment fees on the cost of living and small businesses; and 

introduce reforms that prevent banking transaction costs from unnecessarily increasing the advertised price of goods and services. 

