I'd like to commemorate the 40th anniversary of the Corindi Beach Hotel—40 years in our community. It was best known as the Amble Inn, which opened in 1986, and for decades was a landmark on the old Pacific Highway. It was the last pub for around 50 kilometres. Tracey Byard was there on the opening night 40 years ago. She later became the licensee and is still part of the club today. In 2022, it changed hands for the first time, and Rodney 'Ned' Kelly and Corey Dunn took over the pub. Today, it's owned by the North Coast Hotel Group. Congratulations to Harry, Tracey, all the staff members and local people who've been part of the pub's story. 

