More than 560 local residents have now signed our petition opposing the proposal. This level of engagement reflects the strength of feeling right across the suburb of Fawkner. I was at Fawkner Festa on Sunday, a great event, and the issue was raised again with me repeatedly by local residents. They're worried about the site's history, the potential risks and whether the community's concerns are being properly heard. Fawkner, a great suburb in the north of Melbourne, deserves confidence that any decisions affecting this suburb are based on rigorous evidence and public health is put first. I'm going to continue to stand with my community and advocate for their concerns to be taken seriously throughout this process. Communities should never be expected to simply accept uncertainty when it comes to their health, their safety and their environment. 

