Small businesses are being absolutely smashed right across the country, and that includes in my electorate of Fairfax on the Sunshine Coast. Recently, I received correspondence from a fellow by the name of Chris Atkinson, who manages a 45-year-old business. With his permission, I want to share a little bit of a story about what he is going through. What he said to me was that his business expenses—his wages are up 26 per cent and fuel is up 50 per cent. Keep in mind he runs a fleet of 25 vehicles. His energy costs are up 200 per cent. He's done all the right things, by the way, with installing solar panels, but costs are still up 200 per cent. Insurance is up well over 20 per cent, and you've got increasing freight costs and supplier fuel levies. 

